109: \textbf{A Plano-Concave Resonator.} When mirror $1$ is planar $\left(R_1=\infty\right)$, determine the confinement condition and the depth of focus, as well as the beam width at the waist and at each of the mirrors, as a function of $\frac{d}{\left|R_2\right|}$.\\
110: 
111:     \textbf{Solution}
112: 
113:     \textbf{Confinement Condition}
114: \\
115: Note that:
116: 
117: \[
118: \begin{split}
119: R_1&=z_1\left[z_1+\left(\frac{z_0}{z_1}\right)^2\right]
120: \\
121: &=\infty
122: \\
123: \Rightarrow z_1&=0
124: \\
125: z_2&=z_1+d
126: \\&=0+d
127: \\
128: &=d\\
129: \end{split}
130: \]
131: Confinement Condition:\\
132: \[
133: \begin{array}{r c l}\quad 0\leq&\left(1+\frac{d}{R_1}\right)\left(1+\frac{d}{R_2}\right)&\leq1\\
134: 0\leq&\left(1+\frac{d}{\infty}\right)\left(1+\frac{d}{\left|R_2\right|}\right)&\leq1\\
135: 0\leq&\left(1+\frac{d}{\left|R_2\right|}\right)&\leq1\\
136: \Rightarrow1\geq&\frac{d}{\left|R_2\right|}&\geq0
137: \end{array}
138: \]
139:     \textbf{Depth of Focus}
140: \\
141: From\\
142: \[
143: \begin{split}
144: |R_2|&=z_2\left[z_2+\left(\frac{z_0}{z_2}\right)^2\right]
145: \\
146: \Rightarrow z_0^2&=z_2R_2-z_2^2
147: \\
148: &=dR_2-d^2
149: \\
150: \Rightarrow z_0&=\sqrt{dR_2-d^2}
151: \\
152: \textrm{Or }2z_0&=2d\sqrt{\frac{\left|R_2\right|}{d}-1}\\
153: \end{split}
154: \]
155:     \textbf{Beam Width}
156: \\
157: At the plane mirror\\
158: \[
159: \begin{split}
160: W\left(z_1\right)&=W_0\sqrt{1+\left(\frac{z_1}{z_0}\right)^2}
161: \\
162: &=W_0\sqrt{1+\left(\frac{\infty}{z_0}\right)^2}
163: \\
164: &=W_0
165: \end{split}
166: \]\\
167: At the concave mirror\\
168: \[
169: \begin{split}
170: W\left(z_2\right)&=W_0\sqrt{1+\left(\frac{z_2}{z_0}\right)^2}
171: \\
172: &=W_0\sqrt{1+\left(\frac{d}{d\sqrt{\frac{R_2}{d}-1}}\right)^2}
173: \\
174: &=W_0\sqrt{1+\frac{d}{R_2-d}}
175: \end{split}
176: \]
